# Security and privacy headers, read by Cloudflare Workers static assets.
#
# The point of the CSP here is to ENFORCE the promise the privacy page already
# makes: "Loading a page does not cause your browser to contact any outside
# company." Until now that was a claim. default-src 'self' makes it a rule the
# browser applies — and one that fails loudly the moment anyone adds a font CDN,
# an analytics tag or a remote script, instead of the promise quietly becoming
# false. On a site about the difference between a claim and proof, that gap was
# the wrong one to leave open.
#
# Honest limitation: script-src keeps 'unsafe-inline'. The whole site is one
# inline <script>, so the alternative is a SHA-256 hash regenerated on every
# edit to index.html — and a stale hash does not degrade the page, it kills all
# JavaScript on it. That is a bad trade for a single-author site with no
# user-generated content, no third-party scripts, and only first-party data
# reaching innerHTML. This CSP is a privacy control, not an XSS defence. If the
# site ever accepts user content, revisit that line first.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000

# Notes on the choices above, so nobody has to re-derive them:
#
# Referrer-Policy: no-referrer — stronger than the usual
#   strict-origin-when-cross-origin, and it costs nothing here. The only
#   outbound links are DOIs, and no publisher needs to know a reader came from a
#   page about grey-market peptides. That is a real privacy exposure for
#   visitors to this particular site, not a theoretical one.
#
# img-src allows data: because the favicon is an inline SVG data URI. Without
#   it the tab icon silently disappears.
#
# connect-src 'self' is what keeps fetch('tracker.json') working; anything
#   pointing off-site would now fail visibly in the console.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security is the one sticky header here — browsers remember
#   it for the max-age. 180 days, no includeSubDomains and no preload, so a
#   future subdomain is not locked in and the decision stays reversible.
#
# Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin stops other sites hotlinking the
#   fonts and og-image.png. It does NOT block social scrapers, which fetch
#   og-image.png directly rather than embedding it cross-origin.
